 "_doc": "DEP-03 custody: a coin paying our key that is output 0 of a lottery claim is a ledger's custody until it is spent (rotated into the ledger's vault), and is never pledged, whatever our own records say. Identified on chain from the spending transaction alone: its input 0 spends output 0 of its prevout through a taproot SCRIPT path (the witness ends in a control block: 33+32k bytes, leaf version 0xc0/0xc1) with nSequence 0xfffffffd (a full claim) or the reveal CSV 72 (a subset claim), and the coin is its ONE output (a confiscation spends the vault the same way but has more than one output; a re-arm spend carries a tier CSV). Real regtest transactions (1121-next4c, deposits-rust ref6): ref6 claimed ad87b48b's lottery output e6184d32:0 as 0588521b's (a lottery found by script, before ff5b053), recorded the DisputeAcquire on 0588521b's fork, and then pledged the claim's output fdff3a5f:0 as collateral on 9e23c858; 14 of ref6's 31 coins were claim outputs, 7 of them pledged. Shared by deposits-rust (dispute.rs, claim_output_shaped) and cl-deposits (node.lisp, claim-output-p). hex is the raw transaction.",
